{
  "description": "Add a small gated recent-history residual to SASRec and train candidate scores with uniform multi-negative candidate softmax. Use a four-cell architecture-by-objective ablation to establish whether either component contributes before accepting the combined model.",
  "motivation": "The recent branch targets broad recommendations that displace current mood or task matches. Retaining SASRec provides a mechanism for sustained narrow preferences to remain influential when recent interactions are isolated. These explicitly address two diagnosed user-facing failures, although neither mechanism guarantees success. Multi-negative competition targets weak positive–negative separation, especially Electronics’ negative lower-decile margin. Equipment compatibility, ownership, satisfied needs and simulator traits remain unobserved; do not claim to solve or label them.",
  "implementation_notes": "Preserve DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, four independent category routes, baseline splits, and int(os.environ.get('SASREC_EPOCHS', '200')). Write all artifacts beneath the trial directory. Preserve the actual RecHarness baseline's attention, padding, embedding scaling, tied output embeddings and normalization; document deviations from the official SASRec implementation rather than silently changing them.\n\nAt position t, compute m_t as the padding-masked mean of raw, unscaled item embeddings at max(0,t-4) through t, excluding position embeddings and all future items. Clamp the denominator to at least one and zero invalid outputs. Let h_t be the baseline's final normalized SASRec state. Set g_t = sigmoid(W[h_t;m_t]+b), with a vector gate W initialized to zero and b=-3. Set z_t = h_t + g_t * P(LN(m_t)), with P a bias-free d-by-d projection initialized to identity and LN having its usual unit scale and zero bias. Do not add another final normalization. This makes the initial residual small, not exactly zero. Use identical dropout settings across comparisons; use the same raw embedding lookup for pooling and tied candidate scoring.\n\nFor each user, define the category-local eligible set as all nonpadding item IDs minus the complete training-positive set. Construct this exclusion while user identity is available inside the dataset sampler; a truncated sequence cannot reconstruct it. Draw exactly 64 negatives independently with replacement for each valid position. Keep duplicate multiplicity; exclude no items using validation or test interactions. Explicitly skip and count users with zero eligible items in every experimental arm. Positives are training items and therefore already excluded. Do not also deduplicate or silently shrink K. These are unobserved items, not established dislikes; complete-training-history exclusion also uses later training interactions, so it is a deliberate training-sampling convention rather than an online prefix-only simulation.\n\nUse uncorrected candidate cross-entropy L = logsumexp(s_positive, s_negative_1, ..., s_negative_64) - s_positive, averaged over valid positions. This is a 65-entry candidate objective, not an unbiased full-catalogue softmax approximation. Apply no LogQ or catalogue-size correction. Chunk positions when necessary while preserving the exact valid-position mean and gradients; do not alter K to resolve memory pressure. Preserve baseline optimizer and hyperparameters for the initial ablation. Fix and record sampler RNG streams separately from model initialization; share negative draws between the two architectures under each objective. The BCE control retains the baseline objective and negative count, so the objective comparison jointly changes loss and candidate count and must be described accordingly.\n\nMaintain a training-only batch path carrying the sampled B-by-L-by-64 negatives while user identity remains internal to sampling. Provide a separate diagnostic loader yielding exactly (None, sequence, positive, negative), with all tensors B-by-L and one eligible sampled negative per valid position. Preserve DiagnosisProbe(view, device).run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), returning metrics and metric_definitions; view.model must be the trained nn.Module. view.item_emb exposes its actual item embedding, log2feats returns fused states, and predict_score uses the identical tied-embedding scoring path. Preserve user_train, meta_data and review_data compatibility fields using only available data. Report category-based diagnostics as unavailable; do not infer unavailable item categories from the four dataset routes or invent reviews, ratings, prices or stores. Training margins are diagnostics, not selection metrics; logit scale changes can increase margins without improving ranking.\n\nSave architecture version, window, gate/projection configuration, baseline hyperparameters, item mappings and state_dict beneath the trial directory. Update the predictor writer so working/predict.py reconstructs the exact trained module, calls eval(), disables gradients, applies identical sequence truncation/padding and routes every dataset correctly. Verify save/load score agreement on training-derived inputs. Continue full-catalogue unseen-item recommendations for five real training users per category through the existing simulator path; do not replace this with sampled-candidate recommendations.\n\nPrespecify the four primary cells: baseline+BCE, residual+BCE, baseline+candidate-softmax, residual+candidate-softmax. Declare epoch checkpoints and deterministic promotion/tie rules before observing outcomes. Screen at equal measured GPU cost while retaining all categories, then promote within a reserved full-length budget; count baseline runs, failed trials, diagnostics and serialization checks toward 43,200 GPU-seconds. Optional later controls are last-item-only and recent-mean-only scorers, last-item residual, and fixed-coefficient recent residual; do not launch their full factorial automatically. They distinguish additional capacity, pooling, and learned gating, but remain untested unless budget permits.\n\nSelect exclusively using pinned four-category macro validation HR@10, with per-category results and Electronics reported separately. Where the existing host supplies per-user hit outcomes, compare fixed model pairs on identical users and candidates: bootstrap paired outcomes within each category for 10,000 CPU replicates using a declared seed, then report the macro difference, 95% percentile interval, category differences and discordant-hit counts. One additional hit changes macro HR@10 by 0.00125. If per-user outcomes are unavailable, omit intervals rather than modify the evaluator or manufacture them. Intervals condition on trained models and fixed candidates; they exclude training and negative-candidate randomness and do not correct adaptive validation selection. Disclose all inspected trials/checkpoints and describe selected gains as exploratory. No test access, external weights, new datasets or benchmark improvements are claimed.",
  "pseudocode": "prespecify four architecture/objective cells, checkpoints, GPU allocations and promotion rules\nfor each cell and each of the four existing dataset routes:\n    reset baseline preprocessing/training seeds to 0/42\n    initialize the unchanged SASRec backbone\n    if residual enabled:\n        initialize W=0, b=-3, P=identity, LN.scale=1, LN.bias=0\n    build eligible item sets using complete training histories only\n    for training batch from sampler that internally knows user IDs:\n        sequence, positive, negatives = batch  # negatives B,L,K; K=1 or 64\n        h = baseline_final_normalized_states(sequence)\n        if residual enabled:\n            raw = item_emb(sequence)  # no sqrt(d) scaling or positions\n            m = causal_padding_masked_window_mean(raw, sequence != 0, window=5)\n            g = sigmoid(linear(concat(h, m), W, b))\n            z = h + g * P(LN(m))\n        else:\n            z = h\n        if baseline BCE:\n            loss = unchanged_baseline_BCE(z, positive, negatives[..., 0])\n        else:\n            # 64 eligible uniform draws WITH replacement; retain multiplicity\n            scores = tied_embedding_dot(z, concat(positive[..., None], negatives))\n            loss = mean_valid(logsumexp(scores, dim=-1) - scores[..., 0])\n        update using baseline optimizer\n        stop or checkpoint according to prespecified budget\n    save state, architecture configuration and matching predictor writer output\n    verify save/load scores on training-derived inputs\n    run adapted diagnosis with a separate (None, seq, pos, neg) B-by-L loader\nobtain pinned host validation outcomes at declared checkpoints\npromote according to declared macro-HR@10 and GPU-budget rules\nreport all trials, category scores, fixed-pair uncertainty when available, and GPU cost\nselect by pinned macro validation HR@10; keep test labels unavailable",
