- **`pos_neg_margin_mean` / `pos_neg_margin_p10`**: Mean and lower tenth 
percentile of positive-minus-negative logits across nonpadding positive 
positions in at most ten batches. Larger values indicate stronger sampled 
training separation.
- **`pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate`**: Fraction with negative margins; lower is 
better.
- **`pos_neg_small_margin_rate`**: Fraction with margins below 0.5; lower 
indicates fewer weakly separated pairs.
- **`pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown`**: Counts metadata categories separately
for positive and negative items in weak-margin and wrong-rank cases, retaining 
the top 20.

# Perturbation & Tests

There are no sequence perturbations, shuffles, sensitivity tests, or SVD 
analyses. Random embedding subsampling controls probe cost; supplied negatives 
test pairwise separation.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The raw result contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. A separate 
