{
  "description": "Add a normalized, causally pooled recent-history branch to SASRec, using matched fixed-gate and learned-gate controls to distinguish history aggregation from last-item reinforcement.",
  "motivation": "Feedback suggests that recent, specific preferences sometimes receive insufficient weight. Established long-/short-term fusion methods motivate a small controlled adaptation, while matched controls test whether any gain comes from earlier recent history rather than the last input item alone.",
  "implementation_notes": "Run four prespecified configurations: unchanged baseline; last-item fusion with fixed g=0.1; five-position recency fusion with fixed g=0.1; identical recency fusion with a learned scalar gate initialized at logit -2.2. Use position decay tau=2, excluding padding and including only inputs through each position. Pool unscaled item embeddings. Apply separate affine LayerNorms with epsilon 1e-5 to SASRec and pooled features, then blend as (1-g)*normalized_sequence + g*normalized_pool; mask padded outputs. Keep baseline output embeddings, loss, optimizer, splits, seeds, and dataset routing. This controlled family does not isolate normalization from fusion; avoid attributing every gain to recency. Serialize branch configuration, normalization parameters, and gate; generate working/predict.py with identical computation. Respect SASREC_EPOCHS, whose supplied default is 200, and checkpoints at 50, 100, and the configured final epoch without exceeding that limit. Select using the host's pinned four-category macro validation HR@10. Predeclare deterministic tie handling and a descriptive practical-gain threshold of 0.005. Account for all concurrent GPU usage within 43,200 GPU-seconds and reserve 25% for finalist completion and ablations; no runtime guarantee is implied. Preserve DiagnosisProbe's required constructor, method, return keys, actual-model reference, and compatibility hooks. Restore prior model mode, distinguish unavailable metrics from zero, and leave category metadata breakdowns empty. Use only public histories, titles, descriptions, and timestamps; reviews, ratings, ownership, simulator traits, and item categories remain unavailable. Training-history perturbations measure fitted-model sensitivity, not independent generalization. Conditional paired bootstrap intervals require per-user host validation outcomes; do not invent them or replace the evaluator. No implementation execution or performance improvement is claimed.",
  "pseudocode": "configurations = [baseline, last_fixed, recent_fixed, recent_learned]\nfor configuration in configurations:\n    retain all four dataset routes and required seeds\n    E = item_embedding(sequence)  # unscaled lookup\n    S = baseline_sasrec_features(sequence)\n    if configuration != baseline:\n        for position t:\n            J = valid input positions in [max(0,t-4), t]\n            if configuration == last_fixed:\n                P[t] = E[t]\n            else:\n                a = exp(-(t-J)/2)\n                P[t] = sum(a * E[J]) / sum(a)\n        g = sigmoid(gate_logit) if learned else 0.1\n        H = ((1-g)*LN_sequence(S) + g*LN_pool(P)) * valid_mask\n    else:\n        H = S\n    train using baseline scores, loss, optimizer and seed 42\n    serialize architecture, normalization and gate parameters\n    generate predictor implementing identical scoring\n    evaluate only through pinned host validation\n# Compare fixed recent versus fixed last to assess aggregation.\n# Compare learned recent versus fixed recent to assess gating.\n# Select by macro HR@10; report uncertainty and all attempted trials.",
