Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

Diagnosis inspects item embedding geometry and sequence-conditioned 
positive/negative scores. It reads `item_emb.weight`, computes per-position 
sequence representations through `log2feats(sequence)`, and scores candidates 
using `predict_score(features, items)`.

The model implementation is absent, so its internal architecture and final 
user-representation computation cannot be verified. These probes use 
per-position features rather than explicitly selecting a final sequence 
representation.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(model, device)` receives the model compatibility view and 
retains `meta_data`, `review_data`, and `user_train`. Only metadata is 
subsequently used; histories and reviews are not directly inspected.

The training loader yields `(None, sequence, positive, negative)`, with tensors 
shaped `B × L`. Sequence inputs are converted to NumPy before feature 
extraction. Positive and negative IDs are stacked into `B × L × 2` candidates 
for scoring. Positions with positive ID zero are excluded.

# Probes & Metrics

- **`embedding_collapse_score`:** Samples up to 2,048 nonpadding item embeddings
using seed 42, normalizes them, averages off-diagonal cosine similarities, and 
maps the result through `(cosine + 1)/2`. Higher values indicate directional 
alignment; approximately 0.5 means average cosine near zero.
- **`pos_neg_margin_mean` / `pos_neg_margin_p10`:** Mean and lower tenth 
percentile of positive minus negative logits across up to ten training batches. 
Larger margins suggest stronger separation.
- **`pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate`:** Fraction of margins below zero; lower is 
better.
- **`pos_neg_small_margin_rate`:** Fraction of margins below 0.5; lower 
indicates fewer weakly separated pairs.
- **`pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown`:** Counts metadata categories separately
for positive and negative items in weak-margin and incorrect-ranking cases.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence shuffling, input perturbation, gradient analysis, or sensitivity 
tests run. Scoring uses evaluation mode without gradients. The probe leaves the 
model in evaluation mode.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

`run_full_diagnosis` returns `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. A separate 
interpreter prompt requests JSON containing `status`, `core_findings`, 
`key_implications`, and `evidence`; interpretation is not performed by the probe
itself.

Metrics describe sampled training behavior, not validation HR@10 or 
generalization. Raw margins depend on logit scale and negative sampling. 
Category metadata is unavailable in this task, so category lists should be 
empty. Empty observations produce zero defaults that can resemble healthy 
results. No per-dataset macro aggregation, recommendation diversity measurement,
or simulator-trait assessment is implemented.

