{
  "description": "Freeze each category’s SASRec and add a scale-calibrated recent-history cosine residual, preserving baseline behavior at coefficient zero. Retain the original adapter framework and evaluate the proposal as an exploratory validation experiment.",
  "motivation": "The diagnosis suggests that recent specific interests may be underrepresented, but neither this mechanism nor the utility of additional similarity is established. A frozen residual provides a cheap, reversible test. Fixed training-only calibration addresses the original mismatch between unbounded SASRec logits and bounded cosine affinity; controlled history variants test whether additional history and exponential weighting contribute beyond the last item.",
  "implementation_notes": "Preserve all four categories, preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, baseline splits and routing, and DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR']. Honor SASREC_EPOCHS, with host default 200, and write all artifacts beneath the trial directory. Train on one GPU; account for training, diagnosis, debugging, and failures within the shared 43,200 GPU-second budget. No test labels, extra datasets, pretrained weights, or unavailable metadata may be used.\n\nFor each frozen checkpoint, define age as the number of events before the current prefix endpoint. For the last K=5 nonpadding events, use weights 2^(-age/2), count repeated items once per occurrence, average their raw learned embeddings, and normalize the resulting vector with F.normalize(eps=1e-8). Normalize candidate embeddings separately. This preserves the original cosine-of-weighted-mean proposal; it is generally different from averaging individual item cosine similarities. Use that same formula in every path. An empty prefix yields a zero vector and zero residual.\n\nEstimate fixed scales without validation labels: using a category-local NumPy RNG seeded 42, sample without replacement up to 256 users having nonempty training histories and retain their full training prefixes truncated exactly as inference does; sample without replacement up to 1,024 nonpadding catalog item IDs. Evaluate the Cartesian product of those prefixes and items in batches. Let s_base and s_res be population standard deviations across the resulting base and residual scores, each floored at 1e-6. These catalog items are calibration inputs, not labeled negatives. Save the scales. Score candidate i as base_score(i) + alpha * (s_base / s_res) * residual(i). Calibration is fixed across candidate sets, preserving inference behavior between sampled and full-catalog scoring. Coefficient zero must bypass the residual addition to reproduce baseline scores exactly. Log component standard deviations and validation top-10 boundary margins.\n\nPrespecify exponential-five as the primary variant. Select alpha separately per category from [0, 0.1, 0.3, 1.0], using pinned validation HR@10 and the smallest coefficient on ties; maximizing each equally weighted category independently maximizes the macro score within this factorized grid. Cache baseline and residual validation scores. Report every coefficient’s category and macro results, including zero. Compute diagnostic controls for last-item-only and uniform-five histories, using the same normalization and coefficient grid and separately saved training-only scales. Report similarity-only rankings as well. Do not silently promote a diagnostic variant: any promotion or additional decay-rate search becomes another recorded adaptive selection step. No improvement has yet been measured.\n\nThe compatibility view must expose the actual deployed scoring wrapper as view.model and the learned embedding as view.item_emb. log2feats(sequence) returns a tensor B x L x 2D containing causal SASRec states and normalized prefix-specific recent-history vectors. predict_score splits the tensor and applies exactly the deployed score, supporting aligned B x L x C candidate IDs and final-position candidate batches. Construct uniform rolling sums/counts by prefix differences; exponential windows may use five shifted masked contributions with identical event-age weights. Explicitly exclude padding, zero padded features, and ensure future tokens cannot affect earlier features. Preserve causal and padding-key masks; avoid fully masked attention rows before discarding padded query outputs. Verify Boolean mask conventions for the actual attention implementation.\n\nKeep DiagnosisProbe(view, device).run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), returning metrics and metric_definitions. Save and restore the actual module’s prior training mode. Retain existing embedding/margin probes with scale caveats; add residual-on/off fixed-candidate ranks and negative-outranking fractions. Category breakdown lists remain empty because item categories are unavailable. Represent missing review, rating, specification, or simulator-trait observations explicitly as unavailable, not healthy zeros. Do not infer ownership, dislike, satisfaction, conformity, or diversity traits.\n\nUnder eval() and no_grad(), compare adapter final-position scores with the loaded generated predictor on repeated candidates, repeated history items, short histories, all-padding inputs, and zero embeddings. Assert finiteness and numerical closeness. Compare aggregation with a loop oracle. Modify only tokens after position t while preserving tensor length and positional indices; features and scores through t must remain unchanged. The predictor writer must serialize and reload architecture, coefficients, scales, normalization epsilon, K, half-life, and routing.\n\nRecord every user’s hit indicator for each configuration on the host’s pinned 200 users/category and 99 unique negatives, evaluation seed 42. For 10,000 bootstrap replicates with RNG seed 42, independently resample users within each category and use identical resampled indices for paired methods, then average category differences equally. Report percentile 95% intervals and discordant hit counts. One changed hit moves category HR by 0.5 percentage points and macro HR by 0.125 points. Intervals around selected winners condition on the selected coefficients and omit selection optimism, seed variability, and negative-sampling variability. Same-sample bootstrap reselection does not correct optimism. Keep pinned macro HR@10 as the selection objective and record the entire adaptive search history.\n\nFor the twenty real training users, retain full-catalog unseen-item ranks, supporting history items, exact available title/description spans, relation labels, and abstention reasons. Similarity and prior interaction cannot establish complementarity, compatibility, redundancy, or current need. Any fixed-subset full-catalog validation audit is descriptive and must not replace the pinned selection metric.",
  "pseudocode": "set_preprocessing_seed(0)\nset_training_seed(42)\nfor category in four_categories:\n    base = train_baseline_sasrec(category, epochs=env_default('SASREC_EPOCHS', 200))\n    freeze(base)\n    calibration_prefixes, calibration_items = training_only_calibration_sample(category, seed=42, max_users=256, max_items=1024)\n    for variant in ['exponential5_primary', 'last_item_control', 'uniform5_control']:\n        residual(prefix, items) = cosine(normalize(weighted_mean_of_raw_recent_embeddings(prefix, variant)), base.item_emb(items))\n        s_base, s_res = population_score_stds(base, residual, calibration_prefixes, calibration_items)\n        scales = max(s_base, 1e-6), max(s_res, 1e-6)\n        cache_scores_on_pinned_validation_candidates(base, residual)\n        for alpha in [0, 0.1, 0.3, 1.0]:\n            scores = base_scores if alpha == 0 else base_scores + alpha * scales.base / scales.res * residual_scores\n            record_per_user_hits_and_hr10(scores)\n        record_similarity_only_hits()\n        winner = highest_hr10_with_smallest_alpha_on_ties()\n        save_configuration_results_and_scales(variant, winner)\n    deployed = wrap(base, primary_variant='exponential5_primary', selected_alpha=primary_winner)\n    save_under_trial(deployed, category)\nwrite_predictor_using_identical_wrapper_and_category_routing()\nverify_padding_causality_aggregation_and_loaded_predictor_parity()\nreport_primary_macro_validation_hr10_and_all_prespecified_comparisons()\nreport_paired_stratified_bootstrap_intervals_with_selection_caveat(seed=42, replicates=10000)\nrun_evidence_qualified_full_catalog_audit_for_twenty_training_users()",
