      "reason": "Test whether the main limitation is the training objective rather than history fusion. Strong training pairwise margins do not establish ranking quality among 100 candidates. Seek practical alternatives to uniform candidate softmax, with controlled loss-only comparisons selected by macro validation HR@10.",
      "query": "sequential recommendation SASRec sampled softmax ranking consistency negative sampling bias hard negatives false negatives sparse implicit feedback 2024 2025 2026"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Move beyond a candidate-independent recent-window residual toward candidate-conditioned history retrieval. Look for models that distinguish specific complementary transitions from broad similarity using training interactions and locally learned title/description features, without pretrained weights or assumed device ownership.",
      "query": "candidate conditioned attention sequential recommendation complementary versus substitute item transitions title description sparse interaction graph trained from scratch 2024 2025 2026"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Challenge the assumption that a fixed recent window captures current intent. Seek lightweight models that adapt between persistent preferences and changing short-term interests using histories and timestamps. Compare against last-item and pooling controls; the supplied deletion probes do not establish an optimal recency scale.",
      "query": "adaptive multi timescale sequential recommendation latent intent switching time gaps sparse short histories mixture of experts state space models 2024 2025 2026"
    }
  ]
}
