      "reason": "Check whether candidate attention can reject irrelevant histories, identify closer precedents, and define a valid directionality control.",
      "query": "In DIN-style candidate-conditioned sequential recommendation, how do softmax-normalized attention, unnormalized activation weights, and null-history attention differ when all historical items are irrelevant? Compare asymmetric bilinear scoring with FPMC and FOSSIL, and explain which constraints on query, key, and value projections produce a genuinely symmetric candidate-history residual."
    },
