INFO:self_evolverec:  Report 1: Three starting insights motivate a conservative extension. First, recent deletion lowers training margins in every dataset. This supports preserving recent evidence, but repacking confounds causal interpretation. Second, Movies_and_TV retains 5.05% wrong training-pair ranks. This identifies residual discrimination errors without explaining validation performance. Third, users report both unsupported broad matches and overextended older interests. Candidate-specific historical support could address these two failures.

Three literature insights sharpen the design. [DIN](https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.06978) aggregates history separately for each candidate. This motivates selective retrieval rather than one shared recent pool. [SComGNN](https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.02130) separates relatedness from complementarity. This motivates directional behavioral evidence, although transitions cannot establish compatibility. [gSASRec](https://www.ijcai.org/proceedings/2024/939) questions sampled-BCE calibration. This makes an objective-only control essential before attributing gains to fusion.

The conceptual framework separates three directions:

| Direction | Existing mechanism | Proposed experiment | Remaining gap |
|---|---|---|---|
| Candidate discrimination | SASRec; gSASRec | Uniform multi-negative softmax | Training margins versus validation ranking |
| Current-interest support | Recent pooling; DIN | Candidate attention with learned recency bias | Older but relevant evidence |
| Behavioral specificity | SComGNN inspiration | Directional history-to-candidate residual | Compatibility remains unobserved |

Three minimal ideas follow. Scores are 0–10; higher difficulty means harder. Each cell gives a positive and negative reason. U/M denote user/model diagnosis alignment.

| Idea | Originality | Potential | U | M | Difficulty |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| A: Softmax-only control [gSASRec motivation] | 2: useful comparison / established | 7: cheap foundation / limited mechanism | 4: sharper ranking / no intent evidence | 8: more competitors / training-only evidence | 2: small loss edit / sampler care |
| B: Gated multiscale pooling [starting idea] | 3: adaptive fusion / familiar | 6: economical / candidate independent | 7: current-interest focus / broad affinity persists | 6: history targeting / deletion confounded | 3: small module / masking care |
| C: Candidate-conditioned directional residual [DIN; SComGNN inspiration] | 5: economical combination / established components | 8: selective evidence / sparse transitions | 8: specificity and recency / compatibility unknown | 7: candidate separation / improvement unproven | 5: small module / scoring integration |

Select **C** at 10% progress, using one lightweight residual and staged controls. Each candidate attends to causal historical item embeddings through a directional bilinear score plus a learned nonnegative recency penalty. Add the resulting candidate score to SASRec through a zero-initialized scalar gate.

This explicitly targets unsupported broad-affinity matches and older isolated interests by requiring learned candidate-specific historical support. It targets Movies_and_TV’s residual discrimination errors through candidate-dependent scoring. These are hypotheses, not established improvements; functional duplication remains unresolved.

Compare A, B, and C under the same objective and negative count, then remove C’s recency bias and directionality separately. Select solely by pinned four-category macro validation HR@10; preserve seeds, routing, diagnostic contracts, predictor parity, and the shared GPU budget.
INFO:self_evolverec:  Report 2: Three starting insights motivate a conservative extension. First, recent deletion lowers training margins in every dataset. This supports preserving recent evidence, but repacking confounds causal interpretation. Second, Movies_and_TV retains 5.05% wrong training-pair ranks. This identifies residual discrimination errors without explaining validation performance. Third, users report unsupported broad matches and overextended older interests. Candidate-specific historical support could address both, but relevance must remain a hypothesis.

Three literature insights sharpen the design. [DIN](https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.06978) and [CARCA](https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.06519) support candidate-dependent aggregation. DIN also motivates allowing weak aggregate interest rather than forcing attention onto irrelevant history. [FPMC](https://doi.org/10.1145/1772690.1772773) establishes directional transitions, reducing the proposed head’s originality; [SComGNN](https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.02130) cautions that relatedness differs from complementarity. [gSASRec](https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.07192) motivates matched-negative objective controls. None establishes gains here.

The conceptual framework separates three directions:

| Direction | Existing mechanism | Proposed experiment | Remaining gap |
|---|---|---|---|
| Candidate discrimination | SASRec; gSASRec | Matched-negative objectives | Training margins versus validation ranking |
| Current-interest support | Recent pooling; DIN; CARCA | Candidate attention, recency, null slot | Older relevant evidence; unsupported matches |
| Behavioral specificity | FPMC; SComGNN inspiration | Directional residual | Compatibility remains unobserved |

Three minimal ideas follow. Scores are 0–10; higher difficulty means harder. Each cell gives a positive and negative reason. U/M denote user/model diagnosis alignment.

| Idea | Originality | Potential | U | M | Difficulty |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| A: Softmax-only control | 2: useful comparison / established | 7: cheap foundation / limited mechanism | 4: sharper ranking / no intent evidence | 8: more competitors / training-only evidence | 2: small edit / sampler care |
| B: Gated multiscale pooling | 3: adaptive fusion / familiar | 6: economical / candidate independent | 7: current-interest focus / broad affinity persists | 6: history targeting / deletion confounded | 3: small module / masking care |
| C: Candidate-conditioned directional residual with null slot | 4: focused combination / established components | 7: selective evidence / sparse transitions | 8: specificity and recency / compatibility unknown | 7: candidate separation / improvement unproven | 6: small head / expensive scoring and integration |

Select **C** at 10% progress, retaining A as the first experimental gate. A candidate queries causal historical embeddings with directional bilinear attention and a nonnegative recency penalty. An always-allowed zero-valued null slot permits approximate abstention; a zero-initialized scalar gates the residual into SASRec.

This targets unsupported broad-affinity matches through selective evidence and abstention, and older isolated interests through recency weighting. It targets Movies_and_TV’s residual discrimination errors. Functional duplication remains unresolved; transitions do not prove compatibility.

Stage matched-negative objective controls before A/B/C comparisons, then ablate null, recency, and pairwise directionality. Include parameter-matched candidate-independent attention. Freeze contrasts and validation looks within 43,200 GPU-seconds; preserve seeds, routing, diagnostic contracts, and predictor parity. Select solely by pinned macro validation HR@10. Report paired uncertainty only if host per-user outcomes are available; sampled gains do not establish full-catalog gains.
