Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The probe evaluates the actual deployed `nn.Module` exposed as `view.model`. 
Model architecture is not supplied, so the internal sequence encoder and 
final-user representation cannot be identified. Diagnosis uses 
`view.log2feats(sequence)` to obtain aligned **B × L × D** features and 
`view.predict_score(features, items)` to score candidates at each sequence 
position. It does not explicitly extract a final-position user vector.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` retains the compatibility view, deployed module, 
metadata, review data, and training histories. The implemented probes directly 
use item embeddings and scoring hooks; stored metadata and histories are not 
otherwise analyzed.

`run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` temporarily switches the deployed module to 
evaluation mode, disables gradients, and restores every submodule’s previous 
training flag afterward. It consumes at most ten batches of `(None, sequence, 
positive, negative)`, requiring aligned **B × L** tensors. Positions containing 
zero in any input are excluded from scoring statistics.

# Probes & Metrics

- **Embedding collapse:** Deterministically samples up to 2,048 nonpadding item 
embeddings, normalizes them, and maps mean pairwise cosine to `[0,1]`. Values 
near 1 indicate directional concentration; approximately 0.5 indicates zero mean
cosine. This does not establish recommendation diversity.
- **Positive–negative margins:** Reports mean margin, empirical tenth 
percentile, negative-outranking rate, and fraction below `0.5`. Larger margins 
and fewer ranking errors suggest stronger separation on supplied training pairs.
Margin magnitudes depend on score scale.
- **Breakdown:** Counts low-margin and incorrectly ranked positions. Category 
lists remain empty because item categories are unavailable.
- **Residual comparison:** When supported, compares residual-off and deployed 
scores on identical candidate pairs, reporting positive ranks, outranking/tie 
fractions, corrected/regressed pairs, and mean absolute score change.

# Perturbation & Tests

Sequences are not shuffled, masked, or otherwise perturbed. The only ablation 
disables residual scoring through explicit `predict_score_base`, or a declared 
`sasrec_recent_concat` layout using the first embedding-width feature block. 
Unsupported comparisons are marked unavailable.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The returned object contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. Missing margin 
observations and insufficient embedding samples produce nulls. Unobserved 
categories, reviews, ratings, prices, stores, specifications, and simulator 
traits are explicitly unavailable.

These are training-pair diagnostics, not validation HR@10, full-catalog ranking,
generalization, or sequence-sensitivity tests. A separate interpreter prompt 
requests an evidence-grounded JSON assessment; the probe itself returns raw 
measurements.

