{
  "description": "Add a bounded, directed transition residual from the latest three nonpadding items to each dataset-specific SASRec scorer. Separate source and target embeddings are gated by candidate-specific distinct-user transition support. Preserve the backbone score when independent transition evidence is absent.",
  "motivation": "The selected idea explicitly addresses two observed user failures: broad associations without evidence of a specific continuation, and older interests overriding a narrower recent direction. Candidate-specific corrections may address Electronics’ weak positive–negative separation, including its negative training margin p10 and 13.08% sampled wrong-ranking rate. These are hypotheses, not measured improvements. Neither observed transitions nor text similarity establish equipment compatibility, incremental usefulness, or satisfied needs. FPMC and sequential-rule precedents reduce the originality rating from 5 to 3; sparse coverage and support shift reduce future potential from 7 to 6; provenance, scoring parity, and full-catalog integration increase difficulty from 4 to 6. Objective-only gBCE remains a valuable independent control, while scratch-trained text scoring should follow evidence that sparse transition coverage is the limiting factor.",
  "implementation_notes": "Preserve DATA_DIR=os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], all four categories and dataset routing, preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, unchanged splits, and SASREC_EPOCHS default 200. Use a single GPU and write checkpoints, support tables, logs, and generated predictor beneath the trial directory. All training, debugging, and diagnostics count against the shared 43,200 GPU-second budget. No extra datasets, pretrained weights, hidden test files, or unavailable reviews, ratings, categories, prices, stores, or simulator traits may be used.\n\nConstruct directed adjacent-transition tables from complete training histories only. Define C(s,j) as the number of distinct training users exhibiting s→j and N(s) as the number of distinct users with an outgoing adjacent transition from s. Retain each user's unique edge and source sets. For a training example belonging to u, use C_minus_u=C−1[(s,j) occurs anywhere in u's training history] and N_minus_u=N−1[s has an outgoing transition in u's history]. Because counts are distinct-user counts, repeated occurrences contribute one indicator, not their occurrence frequency. Subtract the entire user's contribution, not merely the supervised occurrence. Apply all thresholds and gates after subtraction. With baseline BCE there is no row-probability normalization; if normalized-transition controls are implemented, recompute their denominators consistently after exclusion.\n\nStable user provenance is mandatory upstream. Training records must retain user_id before padding/truncation and supply it explicitly to the training scorer, or contain precomputed aligned support features. Do not infer users from sequence equality or use mutable batch context. Retain the public diagnosis loader's (None, sequence, positive, negative) contract; a separate internal training collate may carry provenance. If upstream provenance cannot be supplied, the leave-user-out implementation is not reproducible and must not silently fall back to self-including counts.\n\nFor each causal position take up to three latest nonpadding sources, newest first, with weights proportional to 2^(−age), renormalized over valid sources. All three consult adjacent C_1(s,j) counts. This is recency-weighted first-order aggregation, not a joint third-order model; lag-matched C_1,C_2,C_3 would be a separate ablation. Use rank-16 source/target embeddings U,V and\nr(h,j)=A * sum_s w_s * g_source(s) * g_edge(s,j) * tanh(dot(U[s],V[j])/sqrt(16)).\nSet g_source=N/(N+5), g_edge=1[C>=2]*C/(C+5), A=2*sigmoid(a), and initialize a=−4. Initialize U,V independently with small nonzero random values, such as Normal(0,0.02), so neither factor blocks gradients. These are proposed fixed starting settings, not validated optima. The total correction has magnitude at most 2. Initialize no extra causal gate: the fixed recency weights and evidence gates provide a minimal first experiment. Keep the baseline architecture, loss, optimizer, sampling, and epochs unchanged initially to isolate the residual.\n\nAt inference use complete training tables with the same minimum support and gate formulas. The minimum support disables global singleton edges, but does not remove train/inference shift: an edge with two users loses support for its contributing training users and becomes active at inference. Report gate activation and count distributions under both regimes. Leave-user-out estimation prevents self-inclusion; it does not make inference counts identically distributed. A fixed reference-user partition with disjoint scorer-training users would align tables more closely, but sacrifices training data; partition ensembles cost additional budget and are a later control.\n\nEncode sparse edge keys as int64 source*(N_items+1)+target, sort once, and register keys/counts as model buffers; use per-user sparse membership data for training subtraction. Implement torch.searchsorted with empty-table handling, safe clamping, equality masks, and zero outputs for missing or padded edges. Avoid dense catalog-squared tables. Save tables, U,V, amplitude, support constants, source window, and routing configuration. Predictor writing must load the same architecture and implement identical scores. Encode each sequence once, chunk full-catalog candidate scoring, mask seen items for simulator recommendations, and merge top-k deterministically using item ID as the secondary tie key. Do not change host candidate construction or evaluation masking.\n\nMaintain DiagnosisProbe(view, device).run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), returning metrics and metric_definitions, with view.model the actual trained nn.Module. Preserve view.item_emb, user_train, meta_data, review_data, log2feats(sequence), and predict_score(features, items). To avoid hidden mutable state, define an explicit structured feature payload containing backbone states and causal recent-source IDs, and adapt probes to use it; predict_score consumes that payload for augmented scoring. If any existing caller requires a tensor feature contract, provide a separate explicit sequence-scoring adapter and update every caller consistently. Diagnosis batches without provenance can report full-count training-position margins, clearly labeled as such; they must not be represented as leave-user-out training margins. Also report backbone margins, branch magnitude, support coverage, zero-support strata, existing finite-gradient status without backward passes, and counts of evaluated positions. Do not fabricate absent recent-branch measurements. Embedding alignment alone does not establish collapse or diversity; metadata category breakdowns remain empty and review-dependent probes remain unavailable.\n\nBefore costly trials verify directionality, padding, missing and empty tables, repeated-user subtraction, causal prefixes, zero-support fallback, boundedness, serialization, and agreement between sampled and chunked scoring. Log peak memory and throughput. Use SASRec alone as the zero-residual control rather than spending a duplicate training run. Prioritize SASRec plus count-only scores and SASRec plus learned gated scores; compare ungated learned scores, symmetric evidence/factors, bounded versus unbounded scoring, and objective-only gBCE only if budget allows. Match source windows, baseline optimization, training opportunities, and GPU budgets wherever the comparison permits. A normalized-count control may use P(j|s)=(C(s,j)+alpha*p_j)/(sum_k C(s,k)+alpha), where p_j is training target popularity; identify it as an additional scorer and apply all normalization consistently. Do not interpret gains as learned generalization unless count-only and zero-count-pair behavior support that claim.\n\nChoose exclusively using the pinned macro validation HR@10 with 200 users/category, 99 unique negatives, and evaluation seed 42. Predeclare comparisons and log every attempted trial. Where host validation outputs expose per-user hits, retain paired hit indicators on identical candidates, report per-category changes and discordant wins/losses, and bootstrap users independently within each category while recomputing the macro difference. One changed hit is 0.5 percentage points within a category and 0.125 macro points. Such intervals condition on fitted models and fixed candidates, exclude seed/candidate variability, and do not correct repeated-selection optimism. Leave confirmation to the host-held-out evaluation. Do not claim sampled-ranking improvements imply full-catalog improvements. No experiments or gains are claimed here.",
  "pseudocode": "For each of the four categories:\n    retain stable user IDs in internal training records\n    build distinct-user directed adjacent-edge counts C and outgoing-source counts N\n    retain each user's unique edge/source membership\n    initialize baseline SASRec and rank-16 directed embeddings U,V\n    initialize a=-4; A_max=2; tau_source=tau_edge=5; min_support=2\n    for each internal training batch with explicit user provenance:\n        encode causal prefixes once\n        take latest three nonpadding sources at each supervised position\n        assign normalized weights proportional to 2^(-source_age)\n        for each positive and sampled negative candidate:\n            look up C(source,candidate), N(source)\n            subtract the current user's entire distinct-user contribution\n            compute thresholded support gates from adjusted counts\n            add bounded recency-weighted directed residual to backbone score\n        optimize unchanged baseline loss\n    save model, full training tables, scoring configuration, and category routing\n    write predictor with identical scoring and chunked candidate support\n    run adapted diagnostics; label full-count and leave-user-out regimes distinctly\nValidate scorer invariants before training costly comparisons.\nPrioritize baseline, count-only augmentation, and learned augmentation at matched budgets.\nSelect only by pinned four-category macro validation HR@10.\nReport paired validation uncertainty if per-user outputs are available; reserve held-out confirmation for the host.",
