Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)
The probe accesses the trained module through `view.model`. Item embeddings come
from `view.item_emb.weight`; `view.log2feats(sequence)` provides per-position 
sequence representations, and `view.predict_score(features, items)` computes 
candidate logits. The encoder implementation and final-user-state extraction are
not included in the supplied code.

For `residual_variant == "recent"`, representations include `alpha * 
recent_branch(sequence)`. Diagnosis subtracts this term to recover backbone 
states and measures both components.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks
`DiagnosisProbe(view, device)` retains the actual model, metadata, review-data 
handle, and training histories. Metadata, reviews, and histories are not used by
the active probes.

`run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` temporarily switches the trained module to 
evaluation mode, disables gradient computation, runs the probes, and restores 
its previous mode. It examines at most ten batches containing `(None, sequence, 
positive, negative)` tensors. Margin measurements require all three item IDs at 
a position to be nonzero.

# Probes & Metrics
- **Embedding alignment:** Samples up to 2,048 nonpadding item embeddings with 
seed 42, normalizes them, and maps mean pairwise cosine to `[0,1]`. Higher 
values indicate directional alignment; approximately 0.5 indicates mean cosine 
near zero. This alone cannot establish collapse or diversity.
- **Positive–negative margins:** Computes positive minus negative logits. Higher
mean and 10th-percentile margins, and lower fractions below zero or 0.5, 
indicate stronger separation on sampled training positions.
- **Recent-branch diagnostics:** Reports the unconstrained scalar `alpha`, 
valid-position count, average backbone/branch/scaled-branch norms, and absolute 
branch contribution to margins. These describe branch influence without 
prescribing an optimal scale.
- **Gradient health:** Checks whether currently retained gradients are finite; 
it performs no backward pass.

# Perturbation & Tests
No sequences are shuffled, ablated, or otherwise perturbed. Residual 
decomposition measures component contributions, not counterfactual ranking 
sensitivity.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations
The raw result contains `metrics` and `metric_definitions`. Metrics include 
embedding alignment, margin summaries, threshold counts, and conditional 
recent-branch diagnostics. Category lists remain empty because category metadata
is unavailable. Missing observations produce null values; sampled nonfinite 
embeddings or margins raise errors.

The interpreter prompt requests a separate JSON interpretation containing 
`status`, `core_findings`, `key_implications`, and `evidence`. Diagnosis does 
not measure validation HR@10, generalization, recommendation diversity, 
simulator traits, or robustness to input changes.

