Reflection 1: current report is not sufficient because ['The mechanism does not 
explicitly suppress isolated interactions: normalizing the pooled vector removes
its magnitude, so a single interaction can receive the same residual norm as a 
coherent history. Agreement features are evidence proxies, not confidence 
estimates.', 'Both pools include the current item, inflating its agreement with 
each pool. For histories of five or fewer interactions, the pools are identical 
and gate weights cannot affect predictions. Gate diagnostics should distinguish 
these structurally indistinguishable cases.', 'Baseline, equal mixing, and 
adaptive mixing do not isolate the value of two temporal scales. Recent-only and
prefix-only controls would help distinguish temporal adaptation from adding a 
direct item-embedding shortcut.', 'Normalization near a zero pooled vector can 
amplify gradients despite the bounded forward residual. The specification omits 
normalization-gradient checks, cosine epsilon, and whether gate-feature 
gradients flow through the shared item table.', 'The experimental plan needs 
explicit timing boundaries, cap-overrun handling, matched backbone 
initialization and sampler randomness, and uncertainty reporting for the small 
validation sample. The epoch rule is also ambiguous: use the configured 
SASREC_EPOCHS limit, defaulting to 200, rather than imposing an additional 
unconditional 200-epoch ceiling.', 'Originality 3 and implementation difficulty 
3 are plausible provisional ratings. Potential 7 is less supported because the 
claimed handling of isolated evidence is not enforced, and the cited papers 
motivate temporal modeling without validating this particular fusion.'], 
