INFO:self_evolverec:  Report 1: **Synthesis.** Three starting-point insights motivate a small SASRec extension. (1) Causal attention already represents changing interests. A residual can test a specific weakness while retaining that backbone. (2) The supplied simulator diagnosis distinguishes repeated narrow preferences from isolated actions. Additional preference reinforcement should therefore depend on preceding evidence. (3) Electronics has 14.95% wrong rankings and margin p10 −0.4812. These training diagnostics motivate improving separation but do not establish validation performance.

Three literature insights constrain the experiment. (1) [gSASRec](https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.07192) supports testing multi-negative objectives. It does not identify the cause of this task’s errors. (2) [HyperHawkes](https://evazangerle.at/publication/peintner-www-2025/) separates recurring interests and short-term activation. This motivates retrieving relevant history without averaging competing interests together. (3) [Recformer](https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.13731) and [SCRM](https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.14957) use resources or behavior distinctions unavailable here. Their results cannot establish scratch-text gains or verified complementarity under this contract.

**Framework and directions.**

| Direction | Existing mechanism | Proposed experiment | Remaining gap |
|---|---|---|---|
| Temporal evidence | SASRec; prior pooled residual | Recent-anchor history retrieval | Similarity is not intent truth |
| Ranking objective | gSASRec | Multi-negative gBCE | No direct practical-utility mechanism |
| Interest persistence | HyperHawkes | Three causal interest slots | Assignment and optimization cost |

**Candidate assessment.** Scores are originality/potential/user alignment/model alignment/difficulty, each 0–10; higher difficulty means harder implementation. Each entry gives a positive and negative reason.

- **A: Support-gated recent-anchor retrieval — 4/7/8/7/4.** Originality: query-specific pooling / attention precedent. Potential: reusable evidence mechanism / embedding feedback. User alignment: recent narrow matches and restrained extrapolation / no compatibility knowledge. Model alignment: candidate margins change / gains unproven. Difficulty: tensor features retained / causal indexing needs care.
- **B: Multi-negative gBCE — 2/7/4/9/3.** Originality: task adaptation / established objective. Potential: inexpensive ranking intervention / dataset dependence. User alignment: stronger competition / no explicit intent support. Model alignment: targets weak separation / false negatives remain. Difficulty: unchanged encoder / sampling costs.
- **C: Three persistent interest slots — 5/7/8/6/7.** Originality: retention–activation separation / substantial precedent. Potential: recurring interests / unstable assignments. User alignment: preserves narrow preferences / slots may mix them. Model alignment: specialized states / indirect margin effect. Difficulty: compact memory / substantial integration.

**Selected: A**, prioritizing feasibility at 0% progress. Unlike the prior recent/full means, retrieve strictly preceding embeddings using agreement with the current interaction and recency. Unnormalized evidence mass controls reinforcement, preventing normalized attention from automatically giving an isolated weak match full weight.

```text
x = smoothly_normalized_item_embeddings(prefix)
a[t,s] = exp(-nonpadding_age(t,s)/10) * relu(dot(x[t],x[s]))², s<t
r[t] = sum_s a[t,s]*x[s] / (1 + sum_s a[t,s])
f[t] = SASRec(prefix)[t] + 2*sigmoid(theta)*r[t]
score(t,j) = dot(f[t], item_embedding[j])
```

Initialize amplitude to 0.01. This targets broad older associations outranking recent intent and unsupported extrapolation from isolated actions; it cannot establish compatibility or unmet needs. Compare baseline, A, and B within the shared budget. Preserve all routes, seeds, splits, diagnostic interfaces and predictor parity. Select exclusively by pinned macro validation HR@10; report no unmeasured gains.
INFO:self_evolverec:  Report 2: **Synthesis.** Three starting-point insights motivate a small SASRec extension. (1) Causal attention already represents changing interests; an added retrieval branch therefore needs controls demonstrating value beyond existing attention. (2) The simulator distinguishes repeated narrow preferences from isolated actions; reinforcement should depend on relevant preceding observations, although repetition does not establish independent evidence. (3) Electronics has 14.95% wrong rankings and margin p10 −0.4812. These training diagnostics motivate separation experiments without establishing validation performance.

Three literature insights refine the experiment. (1) [gSASRec](https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.07192) supports multi-negative calibration, but sampler and loss reduction determine the implemented objective. (2) [STAMP](https://www.kdd.org/kdd2018/accepted-papers/view/stamp-short-term-attentionmemory-priority-model-for-session-based-recommend), SASRec and [TiSASRec](https://jiachengli1995.github.io/files/wsdm20.pdf) establish close attention and temporal precedents; [HyperHawkes](https://evazangerle.at/publication/peintner-www-2025/) motivates separating retained interests from activation. (3) [DuoRec](https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.05730) motivates checking representation degeneration. Retrieval mass can reflect anisotropy, popularity, history length or duplicates rather than relevance. Recformer and SCRM require resources or behavior distinctions unavailable here.

**Framework and directions.**

| Direction | Existing mechanism | Proposed experiment | Remaining gap |
|---|---|---|---|
| Temporal evidence | SASRec; STAMP; TiSASRec; prior pooled residual | Recent-anchor kernel retrieval with shrinkage | Similarity and mass are not verified intent or confidence |
| Ranking objective | gSASRec | Explicitly specified multi-negative gBCE | Sampler assumptions and false negatives |
| Interest persistence | HyperHawkes | Three causal interest slots | Assignment and optimization cost |

**Candidate assessment.** Scores are originality/potential/user alignment/model alignment/difficulty, each 0–10; higher difficulty means harder implementation. Each dimension gives a positive and negative reason.

- **A: Support-gated recent-anchor retrieval — 3/6/7/6/5.** Originality: explicit shrinkage / close attention precedents. Potential: compact testable mechanism / shortcut-prone mass. User alignment: recent narrow matches and restrained extrapolation / cannot establish practical utility. Model alignment: changes candidate margins / correction is indirect. Difficulty: tensor features retained / quadratic retrieval, controls and export integration.
- **B: Multi-negative gBCE — 2/7/4/9/4.** Originality: task adaptation / established objective. Potential: direct ranking intervention / dataset dependence. User alignment: stronger competition / no explicit intent-support mechanism. Model alignment: targets separation / false negatives remain. Difficulty: unchanged encoder / exact sampling, weighting and memory management matter.
- **C: Three persistent interest slots — 4/6/8/6/7.** Originality: retention–activation separation / substantial precedent. Potential: recurring interests / unstable assignments. User alignment: preserves narrow preferences / slots may mix them. Model alignment: specialized states / indirect margin effect. Difficulty: compact memory / substantial integration.

**Selected: A**, prioritizing feasibility at 0% progress. B remains a strong independent alternative; C is premature. Retrieve strictly preceding embeddings using current-item agreement and positional recency:

```text
x = smoothly_normalized_item_embeddings(prefix)
a[t,s] = exp(-nonpadding_age(t,s)/10) * relu(dot(x[t],x[s]))², s<t
W[t] = sum_s a[t,s]
r[t] = sum_s a[t,s]*x[s] / (1 + W[t])
f[t] = SASRec(prefix)[t] + 2*sigmoid(theta)*r[t]
score(t,j) = dot(f[t], item_embedding[j])
```

Initialize amplitude to 0.01. Since r equals the weighted mean times W/(1+W), weak mass attenuates reinforcement, analogous algebraically to a null-value attention option. This targets broad older associations outranking recent intent and unsupported extrapolation from isolated actions; it cannot establish compatibility or unmet needs. Preserve baseline, A and B comparisons within the shared budget, with diagnostic controls specified below. Preserve routes, seeds, splits, interfaces and predictor parity. Select exclusively by pinned macro validation HR@10; no gains are claimed.
