Results of Code Analyze
# Model Overview (for Diagnosis)

The model implementation is not supplied. Diagnosis relies on the SASRec 
compatibility interface: `item_emb.weight`, `log2feats(sequence)`, and 
`predict_score(features, items)`. It computes sequence features for every 
position and scores paired positive/negative items. The internal representation 
computation and final-user-feature selection cannot be verified from this code; 
this probe evaluates valid training positions rather than explicitly selecting a
final user representation.

# Diagnosis Inputs & Hooks

`DiagnosisProbe(model, device)` stores the model/view and its `meta_data`, 
`review_data`, and `user_train`; only metadata is subsequently used. 
`run_full_diagnosis(train_loader)` invokes two probes. Margin analysis switches 
the model to evaluation mode and processes up to ten batches containing `(None, 
sequence, positive, negative)`. Positive ID zero marks padding and is excluded. 
Both probes disable gradients.

# Probes & Metrics

- **`embedding_collapse_score`**: Samples at most 2,048 nonpadding item 
embeddings using seed 42, normalizes them, averages off-diagonal pairwise cosine
similarities, and maps the result through `(cosine + 1)/2`. Higher values 
suggest directional collapse; approximately 0.5 indicates zero mean cosine, not 
necessarily poor health.
- **`pos_neg_margin_mean` / `pos_neg_margin_p10`**: Mean and empirical tenth 
percentile of positive minus negative logits. Higher values indicate stronger 
separation, including among difficult positions.
- **`pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate`**: Fraction with negative margin; lower is 
better.
- **`pos_neg_small_margin_rate`**: Fraction with margin below 0.5; lower 
indicates fewer weakly separated pairs.
- **`pos_neg_margin_category_breakdown`**: Counts category occurrences 
separately for positive and negative items in low-margin and wrong-ranking 
cases, retaining the top 20 categories.

# Perturbation & Tests

No sequence shuffling, deletion, substitution, or sensitivity tests occur. 
Random embedding subsampling reduces computation; supplied negatives test 
pairwise score separation.

# MODEL_DIAGNOSIS Schema & Limitations

The raw result contains `metrics` and matching `metric_definitions`. A separate 
interpreter prompt requests JSON with `status`, `core_findings`, 
`key_implications`, and `evidence`; interpretation is not executed here.

These probes do not measure validation HR@10, full-catalog ranking, 
generalization, or user traits. Margins depend on logit scale and sampled 
negatives. Category metadata is unavailable under this task, so category lists 
remain empty. Empty margin observations produce zeros, potentially masking 
missing data. Evaluation mode is not restored afterward.

